      "content": "it's just that everything feels too \"perfectly\" erased. like the school records aren't just missing stuff, they're intentionally curated to look normal. and when i try to remember the lake house, i get this weird feeling of... static. like a digital glitch in my head. i found a small printout from an old biotech firm's newsletter in a box of my dad's stuff that mentions \"cognitive archival services.\" do you think it's possible for a company to actually wipe or rewrite specific neural pathways and then back-date the official documents to match? i need to know how deep this goes.",
